<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siddoji Rao Ghorpade</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siddoji Rao <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghorpade">Ghorpade</a> was a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> Ghorpade family who took the valley of Sandur in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> around 1713. His family had served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> and his successors, and his descendants held Sandur as a small principality through the wars of the Marathas, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a> and later under British paramountcy.</p></div>
